itle went to the Philadelphia Warriors, who had no major problems in the final, ending up with a 4-1 record, to beat the Fort Wayne Pistons. Arizin was the...</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2020/03/maxresdefault-2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1955</span><span class="eyebrow">Fort Wayne Pistons</span></div><h3><a href="/nba-1955-final-syracuse-nationals-meet-with-glory/">NBA 1955 Final: Syracuse Nationals meet with glory</a></h3><p>In the 1955 NBA, the title went to the Syracuse Nationals, their first and only title. A very worked, very suffered title, that was only decided in the seventh game, against the...</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2020/03/photogrid_1425675535965-e1425675533337.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1954</span><span class="eyebrow">Minneapolis Lakers</span></div><h3><a href="/nba-1954-final-minneapolis-lakers-clinch-third-title/">NBA 1954 Final: Minneapolis Lakers clinch third title</a></h3><p>In the 1954 NBA, the Lakers clinched their third title after beating the Syracuse Nationals 4-3 in a series that was not decided until the seventh, where the Lakers won by 87-80...</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2019/04/5ccd36a8240000b5002a6915.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1953</span><span class="eyebrow">Minneapolis Lakers</span></div><h3><a href="/nba-1953-finals-lakers-win-strongly-against-knicks/">NBA 1953 Finals: Lakers win strongly against Knicks</a></h3><p>In the 1953 NBA, the Minneapolis Lakers won their second consecutive ring, and this time they did it with solvency, beating the New York Knicks by a clear 4-1 in the final....</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2020/03/1952FinalsAction-bicubic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1952</span><span class="eyebrow">Minneapolis Lakers</span></div><h3><a href="/1952-nba-final-minneapolis-lakers-start-first-ever-threepeat/">1952 NBA Final: Minneapolis Lakers start first-ever &#39;Threepeat&#39;</a></h3><p>In the 1952 NBA, the Lakers, after a year of hiatus, won the championship again. The first of a series of three, in what would be the first major domination in history. The final,...</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2020/03/maxresdefault-3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1951</span><span class="eyebrow">NBA</span></div><h3><a href="/1951-nba-final-the-royals-beat-the-knicks-after-a-tough-final/">1951 NBA Final: The Royals beat the Knicks after a tough final</a></h3><p>In the 1951 NBA we had to wait until game seven of the final series, when the Rochester Royals beat the New York Knicks by 79-75 to meet the champion of the second edition of the...</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="card__media"><img src="/images/bf/2020/03/result.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="320" height="240"></div><div><div class="card__meta"><span class="year">1950</span><span class="eyebrow">Minneapolis Lakers</span></div><h3><a href="/nba-1950-final-the-minneapolis-lakers-first-champion/">NBA 1950 Final: The Minneapolis Lakers, first champion</a></h3><p>In 1949 the best competition in the world, the NBA, was inaugurated. Being the first champion the Minneapolis Lakers, after beating the Syracuse Nationals by 4-2 with a...</p></div></article></div><aside class="side"><section><h2 class="side__title">Key players <span class="side__count">961</s